DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T205000
SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast A Dress Rehearsal – ACT II Cast A (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:Wed. Dec. 9 · Call 7:30 PM · 8:10 PM–8:50 PM · Robinson 
 Center\nMANDATORY — production week. CALL TIME 7:30 PM: dancers must b
 e checked in and backstage by then\, so arrive by 7:15 PM. BA: Call Time
  is the time dancers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minute
 s before Call Time.\nACT II Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair a
 nd Makeup.\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named. SUBJECT TO CHAN
 GE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal a
 re the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1
 xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\nCOSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP 
 for Tea: Chinese Tea — Costume (you provide): Pink Seamless Tights\, F
 lesh-tone camisole leotard\; Shoes: Pink Pointe Shoes w/ ribbons & elast
 ics (clean\, quiet\, unpancacked)\; Makeup: Full Stage Makeup - Mascara 
 Only OK\; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\nFull Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:
 \n•  Apply foundation and powder matching skintone\n•  Light s
 kin tone eye shadow over entire eye\n•  Dark brown eye shadow over 
 crease\n•  Medium brown eye shadow blended over brown\n•  Blac
 k fake eyelashes (note: apply mascara to own lashes before application o
 f fake lashes)\n•  Apply eyeliner after lashes dry\n•  Blush o
 n the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed ou
 t in the stage lights)\n•  Brown or tan on contour cheekbones\, hai
 rline\n•  Use a brow pencil (or eyeshadow) to darken the eyebrows\n
 •  Red or Dark Red Lipstick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone t
 ights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n•  Ha
 ndle costume pieces with care while changing to prevent damage to delica
 te fabrics\n•  Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event of cost
 ume damage at the point of discovery\, no matter how significant\n• 
  Never throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, or hang costumes 
 by their elastic straps\n•  Refrain from sitting on the floor while
  in costume\n•  Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder
  any costume or accessory\n•  Never apply stage make-up while in co
 stume and shall take great care to refrain from smudging make-up on cost
 ume during its removal\n•  Refrain from the use of spray perfume or
  cologne while in costume\n•  Never wear any garment not assigned t
 o cast member\n•  Do not handle or consume food or beverage while i
 n costume\, with the exception of water\n•  Do not remove costumes 
 from their assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n•  Remove a
 ll bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs following their use\n
 •  Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n•  Comply ful
 ly with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n•
   Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that may 
 damage or stain costumes.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT1H
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Nutcracker in 1 hour
END:VALARM
