SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast A Dress Rehearsal – ACT II Notes (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:Wed. Dec. 9 · 9:00 PM–9:30 PM · Robinson Center\nMANDATOR
 Y — production week. BA: Call Time is the time dancers should be check
 -in and backstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Time.\nIn Performance 
 Costumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named
 . SUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails an
 d the BA portal are the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com
 /spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\nCOSTUME
  / HAIR / MAKEUP for Tea: Chinese Tea — Costume (you provide): Pink Se
 amless Tights\, Flesh-tone camisole leotard\; Shoes: Pink Pointe Shoes w
 / ribbons & elastics (clean\, quiet\, unpancacked)\; Makeup: Full Stage 
 Makeup - Mascara Only OK\; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\nFull Stage Makeup I
 nstruction Sheet:\n•  Apply foundation and powder matching skintone
 \n•  Light skin tone eye shadow over entire eye\n•  Dark brown
  eye shadow over crease\n•  Medium brown eye shadow blended over br
 own\n•  Black fake eyelashes (note: apply mascara to own lashes bef
 ore application of fake lashes)\n•  Apply eyeliner after lashes dry
 \n•  Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn
 ’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n•  Brown or tan on conto
 ur cheekbones\, hairline\n•  Use a brow pencil (or eyeshadow) to da
 rken the eyebrows\n•  Red or Dark Red Lipstick\nDancers of Color ma
 y wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guid
 elines:\n•  Handle costume pieces with care while changing to preve
 nt damage to delicate fabrics\n•  Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas i
 n the event of costume damage at the point of discovery\, no matter how 
 significant\n•  Never throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, 
 or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n•  Refrain from sitting o
 n the floor while in costume\n•  Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, c
 lean\, or launder any costume or accessory\n•  Never apply stage ma
 ke-up while in costume and shall take great care to refrain from smudgin
 g make-up on costume during its removal\n•  Refrain from the use of
  spray perfume or cologne while in costume\n•  Never wear any garme
 nt not assigned to cast member\n•  Do not handle or consume food or
  beverage while in costume\, with the exception of water\n•  Do not
  remove costumes from their assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\
 n•  Remove all bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs follo
 wing their use\n•  Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n
 •  Comply fully with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ ward
 robe policies\n•  Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or 
 anything that may damage or stain costumes.
